    "q-223918": {
      "dom_id": "step-q223918",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Expressed as a mixed number in its lowest terms, the reciprocal of $\\frac{3}{20}$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the reciprocal of a fraction, we switch the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{20}\\,\\to \\,\\frac{20}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we convert the resulting fraction to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n20÷3=6\\,\\text{R}\\,2=6\\,\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nSo, the reciprocal of $\\frac{3}{20}$ is $6\\,\\frac{2}{3}.$",
